{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvKa4jaBqc57wvB5tq9A","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Not forever, as long as you keep a test timeout.** The test will still fail, but `expect.poll`'s own `timeout` probably isn't what stops it.\n\n- **Why the poll timeout may not fire:** I'm going from my memory of Vitest's source and didn't check it against 5.0.3. As I recall, `expect.poll` awaits your callback on every attempt. When its `timeout` (default 1000 ms) runs out, it makes one last attempt and awaits that too. If your callback returns a promise that never settles, the poll may never resolve or reject.\n- **What actually stops it:** the test-level timeout (`testTimeout`, default 5000 ms) still applies and fails the test with a timeout error. It only really hangs forever if you set `testTimeout: 0` or pass a timeout of 0 to that test.\n- **How to protect yourself:** make the callback itself time-bounded, for example by wrapping the inner call in `Promise.race` with a short timeout or using an `AbortSignal`. Also always `await expect.poll(...)`. An un-awaited poll can let the test finish early or surface failures in the wrong place."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7630,"cache_read_input_tokens":15764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7630},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"939038db-f081-4918-9711-a78f9c7f419f","uuid":"b55271d7-9f43-4b03-89de-d8a7ee8317d4","timestamp":"2026-10-11T10:50:38.097Z","request_id":"req_011CfvKa4VSHtWTKYLDDUrha"}
